<%#
  A MAKER'S PUBLIC PROJECTS (stage 3, S3-4). `publicly_listed`, never `published`: an unlisted
  project is reachable by its link and must not appear on any list — Public::UsersController's own
  comment carries the argument, and public_explore_test.rb mutation-checks the substitution.
%>
<% content_for :title, "@#{@owner.handle}" %>
<% content_for :container_class, "public-main" %>

<div class="page-head">
  <div class="page-title">
    <h1>@<%= @owner.handle %></h1>
    <%# THE TOTAL, NOT THIS PAGE'S SIZE (hardening, 2026-09-08; tinkerex#279). `@projects.size` is
        at most Public::UsersController::PAGE now, so a maker with 200 public projects would read
        "60 public projects" on every page — the controller buys one COUNT precisely so this line
        can stay true. %>
    <span class="mono muted"><%= pluralize(@total, "public project") %></span>
  </div>
</div>

<% if @projects.any? %>
  <div class="project-card-grid">
    <% @projects.each do |project| %>
      <%# ONE map for the whole page — `#thumb(nil)` answers nil, so a project with no cover needs
          no branch here (stage 4, S4-5). %>
      <%= render "public/project_card", project: project, thumb: @covers.thumb(@cover_ids[project.id]) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <%#
    THE PAGER, ONLY WHEN THERE IS MORE THAN ONE PAGE (hardening, 2026-09-08; tinkerex#279). It
    reuses `.pager` / `.pager-status` / `.pager-prev` / `.pager-next` from files/index.html.erb —
    the component is defined once in components.css and a second spelling of a paged list is what
    the design system's rule 3 refuses.

    NEWER AND OLDER RATHER THAN PREVIOUS AND NEXT: this list is ordered newest-first, so "previous"
    means "the more recent ones" to one reader and "the page I came from" to another. Each link is
    rendered only when the page it names exists, so an edge page carries no link to a 404.

    PAGE 1 IS `/u/:handle` WITH NO PARAM: the maker's page has one canonical URL and the pager must
    not mint a second one for it (`?page=1`), which a crawler would index as a duplicate of it.
  %>
  <% if @pages > 1 %>
    <nav class="pager" aria-label="Project pages">
      <% if @page > 1 %>
        <%= link_to "‹ Newer",
                    (@page == 2 ? public_user_path(@owner.handle) : public_user_path(@owner.handle, page: @page - 1)),
                    rel: "prev", class: "pager-prev" %>
      <% end %>
      <span class="pager-status">
        Page <%= number_with_delimiter(@page) %> of <%= number_with_delimiter(@pages) %>
      </span>
      <% if @page < @pages %>
        <%= link_to "Older ›", public_user_path(@owner.handle, page: @page + 1),
                    rel: "next", class: "pager-next" %>
      <% end %>
    </nav>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <p class="empty">No public projects yet.</p>
<% end %>
